  "body": "Found while working on #3579. mainView (internal/gui/trace.go) switches on `q.Get(\"view\")` and returns a name it doesn't know as it came, and mainURL puts it in the window's address unescaped. So the rule on q can be stepped around through view:\n\n- `view=plugins%26q%3D` followed by 300 characters gives the window a 300-character q, past mainFind's 100.\n- `view=settings%26tab%3Danything` gives it tab=anything.\n- a `%0A` in view makes mainURL unparseable (`net/url: invalid control character in URL`), and SetURL ignores GetStartURL's error.\n\nOnly magpie's own pages reach /api/window/main (apiFramed), so nothing from outside gets in today. Checking view against the names the window opens on (start.js's OPEN_VIEWS, a plugin page's id) before anything is appended would close it. This was there before #3579's patch, which leaves it alone.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
