   "updated_at": "2026-11-02T19:59:19Z",
   "body": "Confirmed on `8abdf53a8`: `mainView` still returns a `view` it doesn't know as it came, and `mainURL` puts it in the window's address unescaped, so `view=plugins%26q%3D…` steps around `mainFind`'s 100, `settings%26tab%3D…` picks the tab, and a `%0A` gives an address `net/url` refuses.\n\nOne commit on [fix/3846-mainview-view-param](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3846-mainview-view-param), `61968cdba`, rebased onto current `main`:\n\n- `mainViewNamed` keeps the names the window's pages go by — index.html's nav (`agents`, `gateway`, `library`, `masking`, `plugins`, `providers`, `routing`, `sessions`, `usage`), `settings`, and the key of every plugin page on (`pluginPages()`) — and `mainView` drops a view outside them before anything is appended. The parameter rules inside the switch are unchanged; a dropped view opens the window on its kept page, as an unknown view already effectively did in `keptView`.\n- `TestMainViewDropsAViewThatCarriesParameters` covers the three carries from the report plus an unknown name, and that each real page name still opens.\n\nRed (product change reverted, test kept): `--- FAIL: TestMainViewDropsAViewThatCarriesParameters` — `mainView kept \"plugins&q=xxx…(300)\"`. Green on head: the test, `TestMainView`, `TestQuotaView`, and the whole package `go test -tags nogui ./internal/gui -count=1` pass; `gofmt -l` silent, `go vet -tags nogui ./internal/gui/` and `go build -tags nogui ./...` exit 0.\n\nNot verified here: no real browser round-trip through `/api/window/main`; the reachability claim (`apiFramed`, magpie's own pages only) is taken as the report states it.\n\nThis is a fork branch, ready for review, not a claim on the issue's ownership.\n",
